    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0500" n="1234" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1234"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mavroyeni Bey.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic">June 27,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your note of the 22d instant, in relation to the interview which you had with
                    the late Secretary of State on April 4 last.</p>
                <p>In the light of your statements it may be that Mr. Gresham referred to the
                    ultimate firman fortifying and making perpetual the concession of the irade
                    issued in January to the girls’ school at Scutari. The firman is still
                    awaited.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
